WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:06.839
Your account, your call: sign out of this device, or delete it for good.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.415
Sign out ends this device's session on the backend at once, clears its cookie and

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:18.795
opens sign-in. Your other devices stay signed in.

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:25.053
No connection? You stay signed in, and Settings says it couldn't sign you out.

00:00:30.971 --> 00:00:35.770
Delete my account says what goes: your email, display name, progress and ride

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:39.061
history. The button waits until you type delete.

00:00:41.295 --> 00:00:46.938
Every session ends at once and the email is freed for a new, empty account. A daily

00:00:46.938 --> 00:00:50.297
job erases the rest, well inside thirty days.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:56.591
Sign-in then says your account was deleted. If deleting fails, the dialog keeps your

00:00:56.591 --> 00:00:57.898
word and says so.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.763
Phone to desktop, the same calm goodbye, and the dialog becomes a sheet.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:17.174
What the tests prove: sign-out ends one session at once, deletion ends them all, and

00:01:17.174 --> 00:01:19.169
erasure follows within a day.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.193
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:27.538 --> 00:01:32.050
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.721
every hill and interval.

00:01:34.066 --> 00:01:39.244
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:39.244 --> 00:01:44.692
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:44.692 --> 00:01:47.682
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:50.520
A custom workout lives under Profile.
